<title>UK: Sema chief Bonelli sells 5,000 shares.</title>
<headline>Sema chief Bonelli sells 5,000 shares.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anglo-French communications technology firm Sema Group Plc said on Wednesday its chief executive, Pierre Bonelli, had sold 5,000 ordinary shares at a price of 1007p per share.</p>
<p>Following the transaction, Bonelli held 104,294 shares, or 0.09 percent of Sema's issued capital.</p>
<p>Sema's shares held steady at 1008.5p at 1330 GMT.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
